# This repo is authored on Windows and runs on Linux servers, fetched straight
# from raw.githubusercontent.com and piped into bash.
#
# Windows line endings would be catastrophic here and not obviously so: bash
# reads the carriage return as part of the command, and a reader on a fresh
# server gets "command not found: git\r" or a `die` message that ends in a
# character their terminal draws on top of the line. Force LF on everything.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
